<script class="sapp-init" type="application/json" id="sapp-config">
{
  "license": {
    "host": {{ shop.permanent_domain | json }},
    "token": {{ sapp_license_token | json }},
    "expiresAt": {{ sapp_license_expires }}
  },
  "debug": false,
  "timeouts": {
    "mobile":  { "preload": "1000", "scripts": "5500", "embeds": "6500", "other": "1900", "async": "3500" },
    "desktop": { "preload": "500", "scripts": "5500", "embeds": "6500", "other": "1900", "async": "3500" }
  },
  {%- comment -%}
    OPTIONAL slow-connection profile. The backend selects it at start time when
    the measured network is slow (window.__sapp.net.slow — from the LCP/document
    throughput probe), or when forced via ?sappconn=slow. Omit the block to always
    use `timeouts`. Here the heavy queues are pushed far back so on a weak link
    the pipe and main thread stay clear during the early-interaction window
    (e.g. add-to-cart, which is LCP-lane and unaffected); set a queue to "none"
    to skip it entirely for slow users. Must differ from `timeouts` to matter.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "timeoutsSlow": {
    "mobile":  { "preload": "2000", "scripts": "12000", "embeds": "15000", "other": "6000", "async": "10000" },
    "desktop": { "preload": "1500", "scripts": "12000", "embeds": "15000", "other": "6000", "async": "10000" }
  },
  {%- comment -%}
    "*" applies to every queue (a per-queue key overrides it). stagger trickles a
    queue's scripts one-by-one with a fixed gap instead of firing the whole batch
    at once — fewer simultaneous downloads (bandwidth stays free for user actions
    like add-to-cart) and spread-out execution (main thread stays responsive).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "queueOptions": {
    "*":       { "stagger": 50, "burst": 3, "slice": 30 }
  },
  {%- comment -%}
    OPTIONAL gentler pacing for slow connections — selected at queue-run time by
    the same trigger as timeoutsSlow (measured window.__sapp.net.slow, or forced
    via ?sappconn=slow). Slow link ≈ narrow pipe + weak CPU, so: smaller burst
    (fewer simultaneous downloads), larger stagger (more breathing room), smaller
    slice (yield to input sooner). Omit this block to use `queueOptions` always.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  "queueOptionsSlow": {
    "*":       { "stagger": 90, "burst": 1, "slice": 15 }
  },
  "dispatchSyntheticEvents": true,
  "defaultMediaTrigger": "scroll",
  "rules": [
    { 
      "match": { "innerHTML": "ShopifyAnalytics" },
      "queue": "loaded",
      "trigger": "timeout"
    },
    { 
      "match": { "innerHTML": "gtm.js" },
      "queue": "preload",
      "trigger": "timeout"
    },
    { 
      "match": { "id": "web-pixels-manager-setup" },
      "queue": "other",
      "trigger": "timeout"
    },
    { 
      "match": { "src": "portable-wallets" },
      "queue": "event",
      "trigger": ["scroll", "click", "touchstart", "mousemove"] 
    },
    { 
      "match": { "src": "E-v1.js" },
      "queue": "event",
      "trigger": ["scroll", "click", "touchstart", "mousemove"] 
    },
    { 
      "match": { "src": "player.js" },
      "queue": "event",
      "trigger": ["scroll", "click", "touchstart", "mousemove"] 
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": {
    "id":        ["sapp-config"],
    "class":     ["sapp-init", "__init"],
    "innerHTML": {{ sapp_init_innerhtml | json }},
    "src":       {{ sapp_init_src | json }}
  }
}
</script>